    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d103-a3">

                <pb facs="0218" n="130" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg130"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Russian contraband of war.</hi></head>
                <p>Firearms of every description (guns, pistols, cannons, etc.), armor plate
                    (cuirasses), accessories of firearms, ammunition and material used in the
                    manufacture of explosives; accessories of artillery trains, of engineers and of
                    troops in campaign, barbed wire, pontoons, military equipments and uniforms,
                    ships, even under neutral flag, bound for an enemy port for military purposes,
                    marine engines, boilers, coal, petroleum, spirits of wine, railway, telegraph
                    and telephone material; provisions, rice, horses and other animals, and
                    generally all things destined for warlike purposes on land or sea.</p>
            </div>
